WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.000
- All right, so the previous presentations

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.170
have all looked really
slick and really nice.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.740
I thought I'd mix it up with something

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.210
that you didn't even know
someone could as a presentation,

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.950
which is, you guess it,
a series of screen shots.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.080
But I have a moderate reason for this.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.440
I wanna show some student
generated content,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.770
but I wanted to make it anonymous,

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.010
so I really tastefully
blurred some things out.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.320
You will notice when it happens.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.713
Let's see, this is, make it bigger.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:39.793
It did it, yes it did.

00:00:43.099 --> 00:00:46.390
I taught MATH 230 and 231,
those are a first year

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.860
sequence of courses.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.800
It's a very intense course for people

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.940
who are usually first years
and they are rather sure

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.440
they wanna do math and they're definitely

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.681
right about to do a lot of it.

00:00:57.681 --> 00:00:59.500
Success in this course and
the major more generally

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.270
is usually highly correlated with

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.900
if you're able to form study
groups in the first year,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.176
if you're able to find
people you like to work with.

00:01:07.176 --> 00:01:10.380
Sort of at university, the students

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.440
are the most important
part of the whole thing

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.810
and students working
with students is one of

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.010
the most important things the
students can be doing here.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.210
One of my main goals
was to try to figure out

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.050
how to get students working
together, how to get students

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.500
kind of all buying into
this idea of a community.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.510
What I did was I had a Canvas page

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.610
and let's see what we got.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.253
It's got a syllabus, boring things.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.850
This is gonna be the page for both 230,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.790
which I did in the fall and also 231,

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.210
which is finishing up now.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.980
I'll kind of mix and
match those two pages.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.050
One thing that I got is some assignments,

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.330
which are assignments.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.840
The first thing I thought the Canvas page

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.940
should be is useful to the students,

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.940
before I can get them to
use some of the content

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.680
that'll presumably help
them form connections

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.330
or help them get more out of the course.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.830
I thought I'd meet them where they're at

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.090
and make it something that
they actually wanna do.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.330
So assignments are
something they have to do.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.010
Usual assignments, they
can click on things,

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.063
see what the assignments are, usual stuff.

00:02:12.063 --> 00:02:15.890
I also have files, which I've
got oodles of stuff in here.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:20.840
We've got assignments, also,
tech files for the assignments,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.110
which just helps them type up their stuff.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.860
It's content, what else
do got in here, though?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.500
We got course notes, which is
now something that they like.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.830
Students like course
notes, as it turns out.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.185
It's something that at
least gets them here.

00:02:34.185 --> 00:02:35.960
I have got a couple flavors.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.180
So course notes are sort of a bridge

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.182
between students being
there and then something

00:02:42.182 --> 00:02:43.787
that they can see on
Canvas where they say,

00:02:43.787 --> 00:02:45.717
"Oh yeah, that's something
that I kind of interacted with.

00:02:45.717 --> 00:02:47.487
"At least I was present
during the creation

00:02:47.487 --> 00:02:49.290
"of those course notes."

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.993
It's a step, it's a step.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.910
Here's whatever the heck this day is

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.570
and yup, those are the course notes.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.880
I was in the TEAL room
which I do recommend,

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.010
it's a good room.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.590
Course notes, they flip
through and see whatever it is.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.300
Some days I did, whatever these are,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.200
these presentations which look
nicer, nicer than this one.

00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:12.010
Oh yeah, cats.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.730
If you have a prime number of cats,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.846
you should do abstract
algebra with your cats,

00:03:16.846 --> 00:03:19.110
(audience laughter)
it's highly recommended.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.383
Anyway, gimmicks to kind
of get the students in.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:26.170
When it starts getting more personal,

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.960
more things they care
about, more communal,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.920
is maybe announcements
and then I'm gonna hit up

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.510
my favorite, which was the Piazza feature.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.600
Announcements, you can do routine stuff,

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.090
like hey, here's study materials.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.530
Or, hey, here are office hours.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.330
Or, here's reading more
if you were curious

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.410
about that thing, you
can jump real in depth

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.270
and here's stuff if
you're curious about it.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.610
Or for me, the always
thing that I need is,

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.360
here's the things I lied
about today, sorry about that,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.613
and here's how to correct
those course notes.

00:03:55.613 --> 00:03:59.650
But then you can get some other
interesting announcements.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.610
Like, hey everybody,
there are free t-shirts

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.443
that you can get.

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:06.470
Here's one of these math t-shirts.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.760
That's suddenly something
that I'm using the course

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.270
not to necessarily
distribute course content,

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.380
but instead to sort of sell the package

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.223
of the social community.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.391
What do I got here, I've got shirts.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:21.950
Here's me advertising an
event that was happening.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.780
That was a cool event, a one woman play

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.523
about being a woman in
math, would recommend.

00:04:30.471 --> 00:04:32.767
Next I wanna talk about is Piazza.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.020
Piazza is, if you don't
know it, it's a feature

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.141
which is an external tool
that can plugin to Canvas.

00:04:40.141 --> 00:04:44.340
The idea is students can
post things, it's a forum.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.560
Students post, they can
post things anonymously

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.720
so they can say, hey
everybody, I'm really confused

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.040
about what happened
today, but I don't wanna,

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.090
you know, slap my name on there
and maybe I don't wanna go

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.880
to office hours 'cause I
don't know, it's whatever,

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.050
two o'clock in the morning
and they just wanna know

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.850
the answer without leaving
the buttery or whatever.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.420
So they can post stuff
and you can get students

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.560
posting questions, hey, what
the heck's going on here?

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:07.930
And then another student can answer,

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.540
oh, I think this is what's going on here.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.170
The instructor can say, yep,
that's what's going on here

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.330
or the instructor can make it more nuanced,

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.553
well, actually, maybe
you wanna consider this.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.790
You can edit everything.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.330
Students can go back and forth.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.270
You can also generate,
so I use this to generate

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.270
not just questions that the students ask,

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.410
but also here's me, I
started doing a thing

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.705
where students will post
their solutions to homework

00:05:31.705 --> 00:05:34.740
because it was partly
born out of laziness.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.680
I didn't wanna write
up homework solutions.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.380
And partly, it doesn't
sound like a bad idea.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.950
Students post their own solutions.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.750
Here's a solution I did for problem four,

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.060
well here's my solution to problem six.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.690
And they can do this anonymously

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.160
and then they can read off
each other, they can learn,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.730
they can see other ways to
approach the same thing.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.600
More ways to sort of build this community.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.600
This was motivated by, I
gave them too much homework

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.430
and then I said, and if you want,

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.483
you can not do one of
those homework problems

00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:06.763
if you do one of these,
so it's a little carrot.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.900
Similarly, they can
post their course notes.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:12.037
Here's my notes for the
day, well here's my notes,

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:12.920
and well, here's my notes.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:13.800
It's the same sort of a thing.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.750
They can be all anonymous.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.140
You can collaborate, you
can make shared files.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.140
Is Piazza the tool for this?

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.040
I don't know, that's what we did, though.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.690
What else do I got here?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.240
Study materials for the
exams, here's study materials.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.570
And oh, here's my study materials.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.810
Here's my detailed study
guide, oh great, cool.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.380
Students are doing a lot of stuff.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.410
But then, they also started
using it for fun course stuff

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.660
like one GroupMe to rule them all.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.220
That way they can all collaborate

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.660
and get all on the same page
or whatever, if they want.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:46.040
So it started out with more Piazza

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.160
as routine questions and answers,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.500
but you can use it to generate more,

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.320
I don't know, more nuanced interactions.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.750
You can use it to then
ultimately have students

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.650
as a communal message board or something,

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:04.510
which I think really helps
with the buy in, which is key.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:05.550
That's all I got.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.595
If you've got any questions,
I'm happy to answer any.

00:07:08.595 --> 00:07:11.390
- [Female Attendee] How often
do you monitor Piazza, you?

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.710
Do you get notified every
time a new post is made?

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.221
- The question was how often
I get notified about Piazza.

00:07:19.221 --> 00:07:20.960
That's in a setting.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.210
I can get daily notifications if I want.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.960
I can get notifications every
time something's posted.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.953
I can probably turn off
notifications all together.

00:07:28.953 --> 00:07:32.580
Me, I have them about,
I think I have them set

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.003
to whenever they get posted.

00:07:35.653 --> 00:07:38.100
Like the day before an
exam, everyone's posting

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.980
their study materials
and their study guides

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.440
and whatever it is, so I get a lot

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.870
of notifications then
and I just ignore them.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.270
But usually, it's a
question like, hey Pat,

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.800
I'm pretty sure there's an
egregious error in your homework

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.070
and problem four should be
something drastically different.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.140
I read it and I say, well
that's correct, yeah.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.300
I've gotta change that.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.822
So those I can respond to
immediately if I feel like it.

00:07:59.822 --> 00:08:01.160
- [Female Audience Member]
So you basically look at it

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.690
every day, you personally?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.610
- I got nothing else to do.
(audience laughter)

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.036
Question in the back?

00:08:07.036 --> 00:08:09.950
- [Woman] Hi Pat, that
was a great presentation.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.010
I have a question about the extent

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.930
to which your efforts to
build community drew in

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.340
the students who aren't
traditionally represented in math.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.940
Did you see that happening?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.495
- That is something that
I very much care about.

00:08:20.495 --> 00:08:22.433
It's hard for me to compare,

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:28.260
how engaged a student
would be otherwise, but

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.797
for instance, it's a
two semester sequence.

00:08:33.797 --> 00:08:37.540
There's usually a big drop
off between the first semester

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:40.020
and the second semester
because students decide

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.330
this isn't for me or I
didn't make any friends

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.540
in the first semester,
so I'm just gonna leave.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.248
Disproportionately, that's females,

00:08:47.248 --> 00:08:49.500
non-binary students, people of color.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.410
It really disproportionately
affects them historically

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.060
and that's not a Yale thing,
that's just a STEM thing.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.248
Maybe just an academics
thing, I don't know.

00:08:59.248 --> 00:09:02.500
This year there wasn't
so much of a drop off.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:06.260
The percent of, the
demographic representation

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.090
at the beginning of the first semester

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.740
is very close to what it is
at the end, so that's a plus.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.950
There are a couple things that might be

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.603
contributing to that but something
I'm keeping in mind, yes.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.713
Yeah?

00:09:18.713 --> 00:09:20.280
- [Female] Just a little
bit on the philosophy

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.860
behind posting their
solutions for the homework,

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:26.593
which sounds amazing to me and
I will definitely adopt that.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.160
How do you go about, is it right after

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.950
they submit their own problem sets

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:36.433
or how do make sure to
maintain the integrity?

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.413
- Yeah.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:44.210
The integrity of it all
is, a big level is trust.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:47.660
I post things, the homework problem itself

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.810
is something that they could look up

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.060
without trying too hard.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.980
Something that they can just
Google letter for letter

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.608
and something close enough
will pop up that they can solve

00:09:54.608 --> 00:09:56.900
and they can just copy if they wanted to.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:01.900
Having students post homework
solutions isn't so much of a,

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.760
oh now they can suddenly cheat.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.156
In my class, they could do
that if they wanted to anyway.

00:10:06.156 --> 00:10:09.320
Plus, I strongly encourage
collaboration anyway.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:12.570
So students who wanna
work together already do

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.960
and they just at the
top of their homework,

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.873
they say, I collaborated with
so-and-so, the other person.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:20.440
But yeah, ultimately I
just kinda trust them.

00:10:21.878 --> 00:10:23.750
I think that's working out for me.

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:27.860
The exams and such are on
par with the homework grades,

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:30.360
so that's an indicator
that something's happening.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.810
Yeah?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.350
- [Male Attendee] So
we've seen that Canvas

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.300
supports Cyrillic and Arabic,
does it support math notation?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:39.770
- It does, it does

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.460
to various degrees of success.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.620
Let's see if I can
magically find one that had,

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.940
there we go, beautiful.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:46.923
This one,

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.290
actually, it is what
it is, I'm pretty sure

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.513
that's the feature that they have.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.900
It supports latex, which if
you've ever tried to type math

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:01.450
in a computer before,
that would be the thing,

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.100
if anything, you might try to use.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.702
And yes, it does support
that, you have to just

00:11:05.702 --> 00:11:08.440
type double dollar signs or something,

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.220
and it just kind of automatically works.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:11.350
So that's convenient.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.950
You could also copy and
paste if you're so inclined.

00:11:16.127 --> 00:11:19.127
(audience applause)

00:11:21.112 --> 00:11:23.862
( music)

